From eb543d2a9f29112064e0057b30a0e156dba561e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:37:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cheeseburger: Wi-Fi for the session and for iOS (boot-arg
 sweetwifi)

sweetwifi=1|2: a kernel thread (started from AppleCLCD::start, 0173) waits for the firmware on
the root filesystem, runs modem steps 1-11 and serves the modem and the WLAN for the whole
session; the watch sleeps (it used a busy delay) and logs rarely after the first minute.
The station gets a thread-safe API (sweet_wlan.h: scan, heard, join, leave, transmit, rx and
link hooks), and with sweetwifi=1 the topaz/HackiOS station boundary (redwood_sta.c),
en0 over the interface KPI (redwood_net.c) and Apple80211 for wifid (redwood_apple80211.c)
sit on top of it (sweet_wifi_ios.c, port of topaz_sta.c). From topaz 0900 (APSL 2.0,
darwin-redwood / HackiOS).
